  standfirst="The releases and source commits that bound the affected firmware ranges, with dates from the vendor's history files."
  depth="plain"
  kicker="Evidence"
>
  <p>
    Exposure is bounded by the firmware that was running when the seed was
    generated, not by the device in front of you today. A COLDCARD updated to a
    hotfix release can still hold a seed created on an affected build, and a
    device left on an affected build matters only if a seed was generated on it.
    The first table gives the affected ranges by model; the second identifies
    the individual releases and commits that mark each boundary.
    <Claim
      basis="reported"
      captured="1 Aug 2026"
      scope="Coinkite's not-affected statements for OPENDIME, TAPSIGNER and SATSCARD, plus the reported one-device OPENDIME entropy-incorporation test"
      source="Coinkite backgrounder and Zach Herbert's captured OPENDIME test report; one unit tested and no independent reproduction here"
      href="/record/sources/zherbert-opendime-entropy-test/"
      compact
    />
    <Claim
      basis="unverified"
      scope="The entropy implementation and runtime behaviour of TAPSIGNER and SATSCARD"
      source="Coinkite reports separate codebases; those implementations are not independently available or reviewed here"
      href="/record/sources/robhamilton-opendime-tapsigner-scope/"
      compact
    />
    If you need to
    act on this rather than check it, start with the
    <a href="/risk/">risk assessment</a>, and see
    <a href="#check-your-device">checking and updating your device</a> below for
    what a firmware update does and does not fix.
  </p>
  <Answer>
  <p>
    Whether a seed is exposed depends on the firmware the device was running when
    that seed was generated, not on what is installed today. On Mk2 and Mk3 every
    published release from v4.0.0 in March 2021 to v4.1.9 in June 2023 contains
    the affected path; on Mk4, Mk5 and Q every published release before the
    31 July 2026 hotfixes does.
    <Claim
      basis="verified"
      contested
      scope="The affected release ranges and source-level fixes in the named hotfix commits, including the Mk2 and Mk3 range starting at v4.0.0"
      source="Vendor release histories and source commits, the v4.0.0 release commit 910e306e with its pinned libngu revision and defined-zero board macro, and the signed-release record listing the 17 March 2021 image"
      href="/record/sources/cc-changelog/"
      compact
    />
    Coinkite's advisory starts the Mk2 and Mk3 range
    one release later, at v4.0.1, and that difference is recorded here rather
    than resolved.
    <Claim
      basis="reported"
      captured="31 Jul 2026"
      scope="Coinkite's currently published Mk2 and Mk3 lower bound of v4.0.1, recorded alongside the ranges above rather than adopted as this site's boundary"
      source="Captured Mk3 advisory and entropy technical backgrounder, both stating 4.0.1 through 4.1.9; the earlier advisory state instead ran the issue through 5.0.3, so this wording has already been revised once"
      href="/record/sources/coinkite-mk3-advisory/"
      compact
    />
